  "note": "Golden blotters. Re-baselined at Task 7 item 6, deliberately: the synthetic generator now carries price across session boundaries instead of restarting each session at start_price, so every blotter on synthetic data changes. The superseded_* fields keep the Task 5 digests so the change is auditable rather than silent.\n\nScore references re-baselined at pre-registration Amendment 3: sessions with no position now carry an idle-capital charge, so every score on every dataset moves. Blotter digests are unchanged and were asserted before regenerating -- the engine did not move, only the metric. superseded_*_amendment3 keeps the pre-charge values so the change is auditable rather than silent.",
  "uniform_note": "Every case pins uniform=True. Task 17 made the synthetic generator irregular by default -- variable session lengths, early closes, empty intervals, volatility clustering -- because its regularity had hidden three real-data defects. These cases keep the uniform world on purpose: they are a fixed reference point carried since Task 5, and their value is that the digests do not move unless behaviour does. Re-baselining them against new data would have thrown that away to record a data change nobody was asking about."
